 "answer": "The most recent server logs are in the `Ollama` folder under `%LOCALAPPDATA%`, in a file named `server.log`. The docs say: \"`explorer %LOCALAPPDATA%\\Ollama` contains logs, and downloaded updates\" [ollama/docs/windows.md]. And: \"_server.log_ contains the most recent server logs\" [ollama/docs/windows.md].\n\nTo open the folder, press `Ctrl+R` and enter `explorer %LOCALAPPDATA%\\Ollama`. `%LOCALAPPDATA%` normally expands to `C:\\Users\\<your-username>\\AppData\\Local`, so the full path is usually `C:\\Users\\<your-username>\\AppData\\Local\\Ollama\\server.log`. That expansion is general Windows knowledge, not something the docs spell out.",
